WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:19.128
Start by counting whether each P is followed by a QRS. Then compare PR intervals in conducted beats. The school decision tree is a memory aid, but its first constant-PR question must not make you overlook dropped impulses that also have a constant PR when they do conduct.
先数每个 P 后是否都有 QRS，再比较已下传搏动的 PR。学校决策树可作记忆辅助，但第一项“PR 是否恒定”不能让你漏掉下传时 PR 恒定、却仍会漏传的情况。

00:00:19.128 --> 00:00:36.576
An origin problem asks where the impulse starts. AV block asks whether atrial impulses reach the ventricles. Delay may be nodal, while important block can lie below the AV node. A longer strip is often needed to establish the relationship.
起源问题问激动从哪里开始；房室阻滞问心房激动能否到达心室。延迟可能在结区，重要阻滞也可能位于房室结以下，常需较长记录才能建立关系。

00:00:36.576 --> 00:00:56.016
First-degree AV block describes prolonged AV transmission with one-to-one conduction. In the school reference, PR exceeds zero point two seconds and stays relatively consistent. It is not an intermittently missing QRS, and not a situation where atria and ventricles are independent.
一度房室阻滞表示房室传导延长，但仍一对一下传。学校参考为 PR 超过0.20秒且相对恒定；它不是间歇 QRS 缺失，也不是房室各自独立活动。

00:00:56.016 --> 00:01:14.952
Review vagal influences, AV-nodal medication exposure and clinical context. A stable asymptomatic patient may need observation and communication rather than rate-directed intervention. New symptoms, ischemic concern or progression change the urgency and require reassessment.
应复核迷走因素、影响房室结的药物及临床背景。稳定、无症状患者可能主要需要观察和沟通，而不是针对心率干预；新症状、缺血疑虑或进展会改变紧急性，必须复评。

00:01:14.952 --> 00:01:32.304
In the classic Mobitz-one pattern, PR progressively lengthens until one atrial impulse fails to conduct, then the cycle resets. Identify the nonconducted P, not merely a long RR gap. Grouped beating may help you notice the recurring pattern.
典型莫氏 I 型中，PR 逐渐延长，直到一个心房激动未下传，随后循环重置。应找未下传 P 波，而不仅是一个长 RR 间隔；成组搏动可帮助发现重复模式。

00:01:32.304 --> 00:01:52.704
Mobitz one is commonly associated with AV-nodal behaviour, vagal tone, medications or inferior ischemia. It is often better tolerated than distal block, but symptoms and poor perfusion still demand action through the appropriate pathway. A familiar benign association is not a substitute for assessment.
莫氏 I 型常与房室结行为、迷走张力、药物或下壁缺血有关，通常比远端阻滞更可耐受；但症状和灌注不良仍要求按适当流程行动，不能以常见良性关联替代评估。

00:01:52.704 --> 00:02:13.152
Mobitz two has intermittently nonconducted atrial impulses without the progressive PR prolongation of classic Wenckebach. The conducted intervals can look entirely normal. Important disease is often below the AV node in the His–Purkinje system, rather than simply a more severe nodal delay.
莫氏 II 型存在间歇未下传心房激动，但没有典型文氏现象的逐渐 PR 延长，已下传间期甚至看起来完全正常。重要病变常在房室结以下的希浦系统，而不只是更严重的结区延迟。

00:02:13.152 --> 00:02:32.592
This pattern carries concern for progression and an unreliable ventricular rate. Escalate early and communicate the relationship and the patient’s condition. Do not turn the school phrase about cautious atropine into an independent drug rule; the current authorized bradycardia pathway determines treatment.
此形态提示进展和心室率不可靠的风险，应及早升级并报告房室关系与患者状态。不要把学校关于谨慎使用阿托品的文字变成自主给药规则；治疗由当前授权的过缓流程决定。

00:02:32.592 --> 00:02:49.104
In a two-to-one pattern, every other atrial impulse fails to conduct. You may not have enough consecutive conducted intervals to see whether PR is progressively lengthening. Therefore the fixed ratio alone cannot prove Mobitz one or Mobitz two.
二比一模式中，每隔一个心房激动就未下传。由于缺少足够连续已下传间期，可能无法观察 PR 是否逐渐延长，所以仅凭固定比例不能证明莫氏 I 型或 II 型。

00:02:49.104 --> 00:03:06.912
Report the actual atrial and ventricular rates, the conduction ratio, QRS width and clinical status. State the subtype uncertainty rather than guessing. A classification limit should increase attention to monitoring and expert review, not create reassurance.
应报告实际心房率、心室率、传导比例、QRS 宽度与临床状态，说明亚型不确定，不能猜测。分类局限应促使加强监护和专家复核，而不是产生虚假安心。

00:03:06.912 --> 00:03:26.976
In complete AV block, atrial impulses do not conduct to govern ventricular activation. P waves and escape QRS complexes follow independent schedules. A changing apparent PR reflects that lack of relationship; compare many cycles rather than using one accidental alignment.
完全性房室阻滞时，心房激动不能下传主导心室激动，P 波与逸搏 QRS 各按独立节奏运行。表面 PR 变化反映两者无固定关系，应比较多个周期，不能用一次偶然对齐作判断。

00:03:26.976 --> 00:03:48.480
The escape origin affects ventricular rate and QRS width, but a narrow escape is not automatically safe. Check perfusion, ischemic symptoms and progression. Coronary supply, degenerative disease and medication toxicity can contribute, and symptoms require prompt authorized support and conveyance.
逸搏起源影响心室率与 QRS 宽度，但窄逸搏并不自动安全。应检查灌注、缺血症状与进展；冠脉供血、退行性疾病和药物中毒可能相关，有症状时需及时授权支持与转运。

00:03:48.480 --> 00:04:10.200
Pacing can provide activation when the native rate or conduction cannot sustain adequate circulation. The school introduces high-grade blocks and sinus-node dysfunction as examples. Recognition should help you anticipate deterioration and request appropriate resources, not infer that every rhythm below a fixed rate must be paced.
当自身频率或传导不能维持充分循环时，起搏可提供激动。学校以高度阻滞及窦房结功能障碍为例；识别用于预判恶化并请求适当资源，不代表低于某个固定心率就一律需要起搏。

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:32.808
BCEHS separates provider levels for bradycardia care, listing advanced medicines and transcutaneous pacing under ACP interventions. Follow your current service authorization and instructor direction. This ECG-recognition chapter does not grant new PCP authority or teach a stand-alone pacing procedure.
BCEHS 将过缓处置按人员级别区分，把高级药物和经皮起搏列于 ACP 干预。应遵循现行机构授权及教师指导。本心电识别章不增加 PCP 权限，也不作为独立起搏操作教程。

00:04:32.808 --> 00:04:53.112
Atrial pacing may produce a spike before a P wave; ventricular pacing commonly produces a spike followed by a broad complex. Some modern pacing signals are small or not obvious. Do not assume every paced beat must show the same large visible spike or identical QRS morphology.
心房起搏可见起搏钉后接 P 波，心室起搏常见起搏钉后接宽波群；某些现代起搏信号很小或不明显。不能假定所有起搏搏动都有同样粗大的起搏钉或相同 QRS 形态。

00:04:53.112 --> 00:05:13.488
Electrical capture means appropriate depolarization follows the stimulus. Mechanical capture requires evidence of a corresponding effective pulse and circulation. Correlate pulse, pressure and the overall patient; visible spikes or skeletal-muscle twitching are not sufficient evidence of cardiac output.
电夺获指刺激后出现适当去极化；机械夺获则需要相应有效脉搏与循环证据。应结合脉搏、血压和整体患者状态，不能只凭起搏钉或骨骼肌抽动证明心输出量。

00:05:13.488 --> 00:05:33.720
Failure to capture means a pacing stimulus is not followed by the expected cardiac depolarization. Failure to sense may cause stimuli to occur inappropriately in relation to intrinsic beats. Both demand clinical correlation; do not attempt to reprogram an implanted device from a rhythm-recognition lesson.
失夺获是起搏刺激后未出现预期心脏去极化；感知失败则可能使刺激相对于自身搏动不恰当地出现。二者均需结合临床，不能根据节律识别课擅自调整植入装置程序。

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:50.712
Ask why the device was implanted and when it was last checked, if circumstances permit. Record symptoms, device information, actual pulse correlation and suspected malfunction. A normal paced rate does not rule out poor perfusion or another acute disease.
情况允许时询问植入原因、最近检查时间，并记录症状、装置信息、实际脉搏对应关系及疑似故障。正常起搏频率不能排除灌注不良或其他急性疾病。
